(7355611, 1150607, 138630, '<td valign="top">Love the scene with one exception - whatever it is that is sticking up from the bottom of the frame in the center.  I''m sure you tried to shoot around it and could not - been there! - but I do find it distracting.  I like the decision to go black and white but the tonal range seems a bit limited to me (I''m on a laptop and traveling so that limits what I can see).  Commenting only at this point - accepting <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30982" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Melethia</a>''s challenge; yours is image #3 in my random display order.</td>', 'Love the scene with one exception - whatever it is that is sticking up from the bottom of the frame in the center.  I''m sure you tried to shoot around it and could not - been there! - but I do find it distracting.  I like the decision to go black and white but the tonal range seems a bit limited to me (I''m on a laptop and traveling so that limits what I can see).  Commenting only at this point - accepting  Melethia''s challenge; yours is image #3 in my random display order.', '2015-06-01 00:30:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7355612, 1150440, 138630, '<td valign="top">I like the tones and the fact that you found an interesting enough foreground for a lovely sky.  I think I would prefer less foreground, both to take the horizon more off center and to lose the brightest rock (bottom left to center) which really draws my eye away from the overall scene when there''s no reason to do so.  I think you may have considered this but not wanted to lose the flowers on the right?<br/>Commenting only at this point - accepting <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30982" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Melethia</a>''s challenge; yours is image #4 in my random display order.</td>', 'I like the tones and the fact that you found an interesting enough foreground for a lovely sky.  I think I would prefer less foreground, both to take the horizon more off center and to lose the brightest rock (bottom left to center) which really draws my eye away from the overall scene when there''s no reason to do so.  I think you may have considered this but not wanted to lose the flowers on the right?Commenting only at this point - accepting  Melethia''s challenge; yours is image #4 in my random display order.', '2015-06-01 00:30:54.000000', NULL, 1),
